    "question": {
      ":question/id": "d3573d29-cf99-5aea-9d53-ca98353732e6",
      ":question/problem": "Calculate $\\int x\\cosh (3x^{2})dx$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let $u=3x^2$. Differentiating gives $\\mathrm{d}u=6x\\,\\mathrm{d}x$, so $x\\,\\mathrm{d}x=\\frac{1}{6}\\mathrm{d}u$.\n\nUsing this substitution,\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}\n\\int x\\cosh(3x^2)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n&=\\frac{1}{6}\\int\\cosh u\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\n&=\\frac{1}{6}\\sinh u+C \\\\\n&=\\frac{1}{6}\\sinh(3x^2)+C.\n\\end{aligned}$$\n\nThis antiderivative is defined for every real $x$.",
